\fs32\b Verification\b0\fs20\par
\par
When all of the lines on the scan have been transcribed, the transcription must be verified before it can be uploaded to FreeBMD.\par
\par
\fs24\b Starting verification\b0\fs20\par
Click the Verify button above the transcription grid.\par
\par
A series of verification boxes will appear below the scan, with one box for each transcription column.\par
\par
The verification boxes can be resized and repositioned so that they line up with the corresponding columns on the scan. This makes it easier to compare each transcribed field directly with the original index entry.\par
\par
\fs24\b Verifying an entry\b0\fs20\par
The first unverified row in the transcription will be displayed in the verification boxes.\par
\par
Compare every value in the verification boxes with the corresponding information on the scan.\par
\par
If the entry is identical to the scan, click the Verified button.\par
\par
If anything is incorrect, correct the value directly in the appropriate verification box. When the entry matches the scan, click the Verified button.\par
\par
WinBMD2 will then load the next unverified row into the verification boxes.\par
\par
\fs24\b Completing verification\b0\fs20\par
Continue checking each row in this way until every transcribed row has been verified.\par
\par
When all rows have been verified, WinBMD2 will display a message telling you that verification is complete.\par
\par
A tick mark will also appear at the end of every verified row in the transcription grid.\par
\par
Once every row has been verified, the transcription is ready to be uploaded to FreeBMD and the Upload command can be used.\par
